    - target: {fileID: 5129102295276735181, guid: f882436c0e514f04392b44e2762adb32, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Historically, the number of lok in a keris represented the status of
        the weapon owner in society and differentiated between commoners, warriors,
        and rulers. To count the lok, start with the first bend on the opposite side
        of the naga\u2019s head. Can you see how many lok there are on this keris?
        Remember: it should be an odd number!"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
