    - target: {fileID: 5129102295276735181, guid: f882436c0e514f04392b44e2762adb32, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Indonesian traditions portray the naga as the ruler of the underworld
        and bringer of fertility, adorning gamelan musical instruments, appearing
        in wayang puppetry plays, and even decorating everyday objects such as the
        betel nut cutter. The serpent often appears with a pointed crown atop its
        head, signifying its special position.
